  "question": {
    "text": "A line makes the same angle $\\theta$, with each of the $x$ and $z$ axis. If the angle $\\beta$, which it makes with $y$-axis, is such that $\\sin ^2 \\beta=3 \\sin ^2 \\theta$, then $\\cos ^2 \\theta$ equals"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{2}{3}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{5}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{3}{5}$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{2}{5}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$I=\\cos \\theta, m=\\cos \\theta, n=\\cos \\beta$\n$\\cos ^2 \\theta+\\cos ^2 \\theta+\\cos ^2 \\beta=1 \\Rightarrow 2 \\cos ^2 \\theta=\\sin ^2 \\beta=3 \\sin ^2 \\theta \\quad$ (given)\n$\\cos ^2 \\theta=3 / 5$"
  }
}